# Who is asked to review what.
#
# Code-owner review is NOT required by branch protection: this file only
# requests reviews. What a merge needs is set out in GOVERNANCE.md ("Review and
# merge"). If "Require review from Code Owners" is ever switched on, an
# approval from any one owner of each changed path satisfies it.
#
# How GitHub reads this file (about-code-owners, GitHub Docs:
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners):
# - the LAST matching pattern wins, so the default comes first;
# - a pull request uses this file as it is on its BASE branch, so a pull
#   request that edits it cannot change who reviews that same pull request;
# - every owner needs write access to the repository. A team owner must be
#   visible and have write access itself, even if its members already do;
# - a line with invalid syntax is skipped, and GitHub highlights it when the
#   file is viewed on github.com;
# - code owners work in public repositories on every plan, but in a private
#   repository only on GitHub Pro, Team or Enterprise. Which plan the
#   organisation is on is unverified here, so until launch this file may
#   request no reviews at all.
# These points are read from the docs page above, not tested on this
# repository.
#
# Adding a publisher team later: once a publisher has an organisation team
# with write access, give it its own folder, below the default, for example:
#
#   /blocks/<publisher>/ @OpenGeometry-io/<team>
#
# The paths in the last group below stay with the maintainers, because a
# change there changes what every block is held to or how it is trusted.

# Default: everything.
